                <pb facs="0170" n="86" sameAs="frus:frus1903/pg86"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Subinclosure 2.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Conger to Rear-Admiral Evans.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1903-07-30"><hi rendition="#italic">July 30,
                        1903</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">Mis., No. 1877.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose herein, for
                    such action on your part as the provisions of our treaties and the protection of
                    American interests warrant, a translation of a communication from the taotai at
                    Kiukiang to the United States consul-general at Hankow, requesting him to notify
                    the commanders of all the United States gunboats that they must not go inland
                    where there are no treaty ports in order to prevent trouble.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">E. H. Conger.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
